---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Screenshot from '../components/Screenshot.astro';
import { REPO_URL } from '../site';
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>A modern, free, open-source mail app that keeps your mail on your computer</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      OpenWren is a modern desktop mail app for Gmail and any IMAP account. It is fast, it syncs your mail to an
      encrypted database on your own machine, and it talks only to your mail servers.
    </p>
    <p class="platforms">For Linux, macOS and Windows.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="/download/">Download</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href={REPO_URL}>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M12 .5a11.5 11.5 0 0 0-3.64 22.41c.58.1.79-.25.79-.56v-2.15c-3.2.7-3.88-1.36-3.88-1.36-.52-1.33-1.28-1.69-1.28-1.69-1.05-.71.08-.7.08-.7 1.16.08 1.77 1.19 1.77 1.19 1.03 1.76 2.7 1.25 3.36.96.1-.75.4-1.25.73-1.54-2.55-.29-5.24-1.28-5.24-5.68 0-1.26.45-2.28 1.19-3.09-.12-.29-.52-1.46.11-3.05 0 0 .97-.31 3.18 1.18a11 11 0 0 1 5.78 0c2.2-1.49 3.17-1.18 3.17-1.18.63 1.59.23 2.76.12 3.05.74.81 1.18 1.83 1.18 3.09 0 4.41-2.69 5.38-5.25 5.67.41.36.78 1.06.78 2.13v3.16c0 .31.21.67.8.56A11.5 11.5 0 0 0 12 .5Z" />
        </svg>
        Source code
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hero-shot" aria-label="Demo video">
    <video
      autoplay
      muted
      loop
      playsinline
      controls
      preload="metadata"
      poster="/screens/demo-poster.jpg"
      width="1600"
      height="1000"
      aria-label="OpenWren in use: reading mail, a warning on a forged message, a mailing with trackers removed, search, and writing a message"
    >
      <source src="/screens/demo.webm" type="video/webm" />
      <source src="/screens/demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
    </video>
    <p class="muted caption">Half a minute of OpenWren, recorded on sample mail.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="reasons">
    <article>
      <h2>Free</h2>
      <p>No price, no account to create, no ads. You install it, add your mail account and read your mail.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Open source</h2>
      <p>
        Licensed under Apache-2.0. Every line is public in the <a href={REPO_URL}>repository</a>, so anyone can read
        what the app does, build it themselves or change it.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Why it exists</h2>
      <p>
        I wanted a good, modern mail app on Linux and could not find one I was happy to use every day. So I built the
        one I was missing, and I am sharing it.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Private</h2>
      <p>
        Mail is stored locally in an encrypted database. Tracking pixels and tracking codes in links are removed, remote
        images stay blocked until you ask for them, and suspicious mail is flagged. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>
        lists every network request the app makes.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="fast">
    <h2>Fast</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Measured with the project's own benchmarks on an encrypted mailbox of 200,000 messages, on a laptop. The
      <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/docs/benchmarks.md`}>method and full results</a> are in the repository.
    </p>
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt>0.6 s</dt>
        <dd>From starting the app until the inbox is on screen</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>0.1 ms</dt>
        <dd>To open a folder</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>30 ms</dt>
        <dd>To search for a word found in a few hundred messages</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>14 MB</dt>
        <dd>Download size</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="pair">
    <div>
      <h2>Warnings on suspicious mail</h2>
      <p>
        OpenWren warns you when a message fails its sender checks (SPF, DKIM, DMARC), when a company name appears on an
        address that does not belong to it, and when a link shows one site but leads to another.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Screenshot src="/screens/warning.png" alt="A message with a warning banner above it" label="Warning on a suspicious message" width={1200} height={800} />
  </section>

  <section class="pair">
    <div>
      <h2>Add an account and start</h2>
      <p>
        Enter your address and password for an IMAP account, or your Gmail address and an app password. Passwords are
        kept in the system keyring. The <a href="/docs/">docs</a> cover accounts, keyboard shortcuts and search.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Screenshot src="/screens/welcome.png" alt="The welcome screen, where you add your first account" label="Welcome screen" width={1200} height={800} />
  </section>

  <section class="rust">
    <h2>Built with Rust</h2>
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt>Rust core</dt>
        <dd>Sync, mail parsing, search and sending are written in Rust.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Tauri 2</dt>
        <dd>The window uses the system's WebKitGTK instead of shipping a browser, so the download is about 14 MB.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>SQLite</dt>
        <dd>Mail is stored in SQLite, encrypted with SQLCipher. Search uses the FTS5 full-text index.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>React and TypeScript</dt>
        <dd>The interface is written in React and TypeScript.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="stars">
    <h2>Star the project</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      A star on GitHub is the simplest way to help OpenWren get found.
      <a href={REPO_URL}>Star it on GitHub</a>.
    </p>
    <a href="https://www.star-history.com/?repos=vincegher%2Fopenwren&type=date&legend=top-left">
      <picture>
        <source
          media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"
          srcset="https://api.star-history.com/chart?repos=vincegher/openwren&type=date&theme=dark&legend=top-left"
        />
        <img
          alt="Chart of the project's GitHub stars over time"
          src="https://api.star-history.com/chart?repos=vincegher/openwren&type=date&legend=top-left"
          loading="lazy"
          width="800"
          height="533"
        />
      </picture>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="closing">
    <h2>Get OpenWren</h2>
    <p class="muted">For Linux (Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora and an AppImage), macOS and Windows.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="/download/">Download</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .platforms {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .hero-shot {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .hero-shot video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .hero-shot .caption {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .reasons {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 0 40px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .reasons article {
    padding: 24px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .reasons h2,
  .pair h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 24px 40px;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .rust {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .rust dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 20px 32px;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
  }
  .rust dt {
    font-weight: 620;
  }
  .rust dd {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
  .fast {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .fast dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr));
    gap: 20px 32px;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
  }
  .fast dt {
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    font-weight: 680;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .fast dd {
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
  .stars {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .stars img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 640px;
    height: auto;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .closing {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding: 28px 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .closing h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
